; the settings and key in ENVARC:Claude are yours and stay
; C:ClaudeCode: the second program of Claude.lha 1.0, one app since CL1; an old copy goes too
Delete >NIL: C:Claude C:ClaudeCode QUIET
; C:uptelnet is up-term.lha's program too: it stays while UP-Term is installed (its Uninstall
; removes it when no Claude record is left)
Assign >NIL: UP-Term: EXISTS
If WARN
  Delete >NIL: C:uptelnet QUIET
EndIf
; the quick-launch icons in UP-Term: (only when there is an UP-Term: to look in)
Assign >NIL: UP-Term: EXISTS
If NOT WARN
; @include dist/common/resolve-uptreal.dos
  Delete >NIL: UPTREAL:Claude UPTREAL:Claude.info UPTREAL:ClaudeCode UPTREAL:ClaudeCode.info QUIET
  Assign >NIL: UPTREAL:
EndIf
; C:wasabid: ours only (the marker Claude's install wrote), and not while the base kit's block in
; S:User-Startup starts it at boot (that kit's Install took it over). The session daemon of a
; running uptelnet ends with that login; one still running keeps the file busy, so it is left.
If EXISTS ENVARC:upkg/up-claude/wasabid
  Search >NIL: S:User-Startup "C:wasabid"
  If WARN
    Delete >NIL: C:wasabid QUIET
  EndIf
  Delete >NIL: ENVARC:upkg/up-claude/wasabid QUIET
EndIf
